From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 18:46:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(build): reserve 16 MB of stack; KD-07

v0.2.0 shipped a build that died with STATUS_STACK_OVERFLOW inside
libghostty on a font-size change. Its release is withdrawn.

WindowsTerminal.exe linked with MSVC's default 1 MB reserve. Zig-built
code assumes Zig's 16 MiB, and a DLL has no stack of its own - its PE
SizeOfStackReserve is ignored - so a synchronous call from a WT-owned
thread into libghostty runs on that thread's stack.

The fourth instance of PLAN.md's 2026-08-04 note, after ghostty_init,
the first WT launch, and ghostty_surface_preedit. Those three were each
fixed by wrapping the one call in RunWithEngineStack. That is opt-in, and
forgetting it crashes on someone else's machine, so this replaces the
rule with a property of the binary.

Measured, holding everything else constant:

  1 MB  + stock              crash at zoom 11
  1 MB  + set_size wrapped   crash at zoom 12-13
  16 MB + wrapped            passes
  16 MB + stock              passes

The second line is why this is a linker setting and not another wrapper:
wrapping the most plausible call site did not fix it, and the path that
actually overflows is still unidentified. The last line shows the wrapper
is redundant once the reserve is raised, so it was reverted rather than
kept for luck.

Cost: this does not upstream. microsoft/terminal has no reason to raise
its stack for our engine.
---
 .../WindowsTerminal/WindowsTerminal.vcxproj   | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/WindowsTerminal/WindowsTerminal.vcxproj b/src/cascadia/WindowsTerminal/WindowsTerminal.vcxproj
index 5135d643f..6f6de9a0e 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/WindowsTerminal/WindowsTerminal.vcxproj
+++ b/src/cascadia/WindowsTerminal/WindowsTerminal.vcxproj
@@ -132,6 +132,32 @@
   <ItemDefinitionGroup>
     <Link>
       <GenerateWindowsMetadata>false</GenerateWindowsMetadata>
+      <!-- 16 MB stack reserve, because this fork loads libghostty.
+           Zig-built code assumes Zig's 16 MiB default; MSVC's 1 MB is the
+           outlier, and any synchronous call from a WT-owned thread into
+           libghostty runs on the caller's stack - a DLL has no stack of its
+           own, and its PE header's SizeOfStackReserve is ignored.
+
+           Reserve is address space, not commit: SizeOfStackCommit stays 4 KB
+           and pages are committed on demand, so this costs essentially no
+           memory. Measured at ~70 threads in a running pane, 70 x 16 MB is
+           reserved VA against x64's 128 TB.
+
+           This replaces a rule with a fact. GhosttyEngine::RunWithEngineStack
+           hops onto a big-stack thread per call, which works but is opt-in, and
+           forgetting it produces a crash that only appears on some machines -
+           four times now: ghostty_init (Phase 0), the first WT launch
+           (Phase 5), ghostty_surface_preedit (Phase 6), and KD-07, which
+           shipped in v0.2.0 and crashed on a font-size change.
+
+           KD-07 is also why this is here rather than another wrapper: wrapping
+           the most plausible call site (ghostty_surface_set_size) was measured
+           NOT to fix it, while this does - verified with the gate in
+           scripts\smoke-release.ps1 against the exact build that crashed.
+
+           The cost is upstreamability: microsoft/terminal has no reason to
+           raise its stack for our engine, so this patch does not travel. -->
+      <StackReserveSize>16777216</StackReserveSize>
     </Link>
   </ItemDefinitionGroup>
 
